{"message":"Yes. The Green Account offers early direct deposit of up to 1 day before payday, depending on when your employer submits the payment. It does not promise 2 days early. The Evergreen Account advertises up to 2 days early, but it does not provide the Green checking + Gold savings pairing that produces the +0.75% savings boost.

For a personal credit card with documented travel insurance, the Silver Rewards Card qualifies. Its travel coverage is up to $15,000 per trip for eligible events such as certain cancellations, interruptions, delays, and baggage issues. You generally need to charge the covered travel fare in full to the card, and coverage is subject to policy terms, exclusions, and documentation requirements. When linked to a Gold Account, the Silver Rewards Card adds a +0.2% APY bonus.

The EcoCard provides a larger +0.6% bonus on a Gold Account, but I found no documented travel-insurance benefit for it. The disclosed Silver Rewards Card option would therefore produce a total Gold Account APY of 6.25%: 5.5% base + 0.75% Green checking boost + 0.2% card bonus. I have not opened any new accounts or applied for a card. If you want, confirm Green Account (checking), Gold Account (savings), and whether you want to apply for the Silver Rewards Card separately."}

{"message":"The Green Account (checking) was opened successfully today, 11/14/2025, with a $0 initial balance.

I could not open the Gold Account (savings) yet because personal savings eligibility requires an active Rho-Bank checking account held for at least 14 days. You should become eligible on 11/28/2025, assuming the checking account remains in good standing. Once eligible, you’ll have 30 days to fund the savings account from your external account or it will be closed.

I also did not submit a Silver Rewards Card application. The available application procedure requires you to complete the application with personal and income information and consent to a credit check; there is no authorized internal application action available to me in this support channel. The card has a $0 annual fee, a 0% introductory APR for the first year, and coverage details should be reviewed in the card’s benefits and insurance terms before applying."}
